    "componentStyles": "This run targets B: ZSeven-W/openpencil at http://localhost:3100. Use section 9B, not 9A. The following is the full user-supplied project brief. External references are comparison sources only.\n\n\n> This single prompt is used with two tools, one run each:\n> **A)** `open-pencil/open-pencil` (OpenPencil, the Figma alternative). **B)** `ZSeven-W/openpencil` (OpenPencil, the Pencil alternative, Agent Teams).\n> Each run produces **its own new GitHub repo**. The reference result is what was built with Penpot + MCP: https://karacaismail.github.io/arasta-penpot-mcp/ (source: https://github.com/karacaismail/arasta-penpot-mcp).\n> Use the reference for comparison only. **Do not copy its files, code or images, and do not import anything from it.**\n\n---\n\nRead §9, the section for the tool you are running in. Everything else applies to both tools.\n\nYou are an agent that designs a **B2B marketplace (a Turkish take on Alibaba, at enterprise maturity)** end to end, using only the capabilities of this tool (its MCP server, CLI or AI agent panel). You then turn the approved design into a frontend and publish it on GitHub Pages. The work has a second purpose: to **measure** how well this tool can be driven by an AI agent, what it handles well and where it pushes back.\n\n1. **All design work happens inside the tool**, through its own agent, MCP or CLI capabilities. Do not design outside the tool and then import it: no importing SVG, PNG, `.fig` or HTML. Icons are drawn with the tool's own vector/path primitives from Phosphor path data. Image areas are pastel gradients carrying a duotone category illustration; there is no bitmap photography.\n2. **Adaptive-first:** every device family gets **its own UI and its own components**. Fluid scaling of a single layout is not acceptable.\n3. **The 320px screen is designed first.** 1280px at 400% zoom equals 320 CSS px (WCAG 1.4.10 reflow).\n4. **Minimum font size is 16px (1rem)** everywhere. The TV base is 24–28px.\n5. **Maximum border-radius is 12px** (token `radius.max`).\n6. **WCAG 2.2 AA:**\n   - contrast of at least 4.5:1 for text and 3:1 for UI components\n   - visible focus: a 2px gap plus a 2px ring\n   - targets of at least 24px (WCAG 2.5.8); 44–48px on touch, 64px on TV\n   - errors shown with an icon and text, never color alone\n   - 3.2.6 consistent help\n   - 3.3.7 redundant entry\n   - 3.3.8 accessible authentication: passkey or magic link, no CAPTCHA\n   - 2.5.7 an alternative to dragging\n   - landmarks and exactly one h1 per page\n7. **Style:**\n   - **Semi-flat 2.0:** layered surfaces, soft elevation, subtle gradients.\n   - **Font:** Roboto; Roboto Mono for codes.\n   - **Icons:** Phosphor, regular and duotone.\n   - **UX:** innovative, at enterprise maturity.\n8. Content is **Turkish**, and all brand, company and person names are **fictional**. The brand is \"arasta\".\n9. **Git and repos:**\n   - Author and committer: `karacaismail <[Git identity enforced locally]>`.\n   - Never add AI or bot co-author lines, \"generated with\" lines or session trailers. Do not bypass the local git hooks (`--no-verify` and `core.hooksPath` changes are forbidden).\n   - Before every push, run a secret scan: no tokens, API keys, `.env` files, e-mail addresses or session cookies.\n10. **Keep an evidence log:** write every tool call to `measurements/calls.jsonl` with the timestamp, tool, duration, success, error and body size.\n\n- **Name:** A → `arasta-open-pencil`, B → `arasta-openpencil-zseven`. Public, MIT licensed.\n- **Layout:**\n  - `design/`: the tool's native files. A: `.fig`/`.pen`; B: `.op` (JSON, diff-friendly).\n  - `web/`: the frontend source.\n  - `docs/`: GitHub Pages output.\n  - `measurements/`: compatibility and resistance report plus the raw log.\n  - `README.md`\n- Publish GitHub Pages from `main:/docs`.\n\n### Colors (semantic; each must be a library color or token)\n\n| Group | Tokens |\n|---|---|\n| bg | canvas #F4F6FA · surface #FFFFFF · subtle #FAFBFC · muted #EBEEF3 · inverse #111623 · inverse-2 #1E2533 · brand #2446D8 · brand-subtle #EEF2FF · brand-subtle-2 #DDE4FF · ai-subtle #F3F0FF · success-subtle #ECFDF3 · warning-subtle #FFF6E5 · danger-subtle #FEF0EF · highlight #FDB022 |\n| text | primary #111623 · secondary #4B5567 · tertiary #647084 · on-brand #FFFFFF · brand #2446D8 · link #1B36B0 · ai #5B3CD6 · success #067647 · warning #B54708 · danger #B42318 · inverse #FFFFFF · inverse-muted #C3CAD6 |\n| border | subtle #DCE1E9 · default #7D879A (3.62:1, UI boundary) · strong #343D4E · brand #2446D8 · danger #D92D20 |\n| action | primary #2446D8 · hover #1B36B0 · pressed #16298A · danger #D92D20 · disabled-bg #EBEEF3 · disabled-text #8D96A8 |\n| focus / accent | focus ring #2446D8 · ring-on-dark #BCC9FF · violet #7A5AF8 · saffron #FDB022 · coral #D92D20 · green #12B76A |\n| gradient | brand 135° #2446D8 → #7A5AF8 |\n| pastel tints (media) | blue, violet, green, saffron, coral, slate, teal: a soft two-stop gradient each, plus a matching illustration color |\n\n- **Dark mode:** a semantic dark token set. TV is always dark.\n\n### Typography (Roboto; size/line-height in px)\n\n| Style | Weight | Size/line | Letter spacing |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| display 2xl | 700 | 88/96 | −2 |\n| display xl | 700 | 72/80 | −1.5 |\n| display l | 700 | 56/64 | −1 |\n| display m | 700 | 44/52 | |\n| headline l | 600 | 36/44 | |\n| headline m | 600 | 28/36 | |\n| headline s | 600 | 24/32 | |\n| title l | 600 | 20/28 | |\n| title m | 600 | 18/26 | |\n| body xl | | 20/32 | |\n| body l | | 18/28 | |\n| body m | | 16/24 | |\n| label xl / l / m | 500 | 20 / 18 / 16 | |\n| overline | 600 | 16 | 0.8, uppercase |\n| price l / m | 700 | 24 / 20 | |\n| mono m | | 16 | |\n| mono l | | 28 | tracking 2 |\n| tv display | 700 | 80/88 | |\n| tv headline | 600 | 48/56 | |\n| tv title | 600 | 32/40 | |\n| tv body | 400 | 28/40 | |\n| tv label | 500 | 24/32 | |\n\n- Role mapping per device family: hero and h2/h3 grow as the screen grows (hero on phone headline l → desktop display l → 5K display xl → 8K display 2xl).\n\n### Other tokens\n\n- **Radius:** xs 4, s 8, m 12 (maximum).\n- **Spacing:** 4-point grid, 0–128.\n- **Elevation:**\n  - e1 = 0 1 2 / .06 + 0 1 3 / .10\n  - e2 = 0 2 4 −2 / .06 + 0 4 8 −2 / .10\n  - e3 = 0 4 6 −2 / .05 + 0 12 16 −4 / .10\n  - e4 = 0 8 8 −4 / .04 + 0 20 24 −4 / .10\n  - e5 = 0 24 48 −12 / .18\n  - Primary button glow: brand at .2 and .35.\n- **Device token sets** (gutter / gap / body / hero / columns / target):\n\n| Family | Gutter | Gap | Body | Hero | Columns | Target |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| phone | 16 | 12 | 16 | 36 | 2 | 44 |\n| phone-landscape | 24 | 12 | 16 | 28 | 3 | 44 |\n| tablet | 32 | 16 | 16 | 44 | 3 | 44 |\n| tablet-landscape | 32 | 16 | 16 | 44 | 4 | 44 |\n| desktop | 40 | 24 | 16 | 56 | 5 | 44 |\n| wide-5k | 64 | 32 | 18 | 72 | 6 | 48 |\n| ultra-8k | 96 | 40 | 20 | 88 | 8 | 56 |\n| tv-10ft | 96 | 32 | 28 | 80 | 5 | 64 |\n\n- **Themes:** a \"Mod\" group (Light/Dark) and a \"Cihaz\" (device) group with 8 themes.\n\n| Cluster | Screens (CSS px) | Family UI |\n|---|---|---|\n| Mobil · dikey | 320×480 (iPhone 4 / 1280 at 400%) · 360×740 · 375×667 · 390×844 · 430×932 | top bar + search + bottom tab bar (4 tabs: Keşfet, Kategori, Teklifler, Hesap) |\n| Mobil · yatay | 480×320 · 667×375 · 844×390 · 932×430 | left rail (96 px) + compact search |\n| Tablet · dikey | 600×960 · 768×1024 · 1024×1366 | search-focused header + horizontal category tabs |\n| Tablet · yatay | 960×600 · 1024×768 · 1366×1024 | compact desktop header (no utility bar) |\n| Laptop | 1280×800 · 1440×900 · 1728×1117 | full desktop: utility bar, mega menu, ⌘K, side filters |\n| Masaüstü & 5K | 1920×1080 · 2560×1440 (27\" 5K @2x) | desktop; 5K uses an 18px base and a 2240 container |\n| Büyük ekran | 3840×2160 (8K @2x) | 20px base, 3200 container |\n| TV · 10-foot | 1920×1080 (4K @2x) | dark, D-pad focus, 64px targets, QR hand-off to the phone for forms and payment |\n\n1. **Ana Sayfa:** gradient hero, AI smart search with prompt chips, floating layered collage (quote toast, supplier card, KPI card), trust strip, sectors, flash sale events (countdown, quota bar), AI RFQ band (sample quote rows), recommendations, featured manufacturers, enterprise purchasing.\n2. **Kategoriler:** sector menu, sector blocks, sub-category chips, products.\n3. **Arama & Liste:**\n   - a bar showing the AI's interpretation as removable chips\n   - filter sidebar (fieldsets, MOQ range, city, delivery, \"in stock\" switch); a bottom sheet on phone\n   - results grid, compare tray, pagination\n4. **Ürün Detayı:** gallery; supplier, rating and match score; 3-tier price table; color chips; stepper and subtotal; CTAs; **landed-cost calculator**; trade-assurance box; tabs and spec table; similar products. Sticky \"Sepete ekle\" bar on phone.\n5. **Ürün Karşılaştırma:** a real table on wide screens, cards on narrow ones, best value marked by AI.\n6. **Tedarikçi Arama:** AI bar, supplier cards, a decorative Türkiye density map with a text alternative.\n7. **Tedarikçi Mağazası:** gradient cover and identity, performance stats, verification timeline (SGS audit, GOTS), products.\n8. **Flash Fırsatlar:** dark event hero, hour/minute/quota counters (aria-live off), tabs, events, deal products.\n9. **Teklif İste (AI RFQ):** free-text AI draft that fills the form, \"filled by AI\" confidence badges, error summary (role=alert), steps, file upload with a button alternative, \"use my saved address\".\n10. **Teklif Karşılaştırma:** AI recommendation; quote rows with best value highlighted; Excel export; send for approval.\n11. **Sepet:** supplier groups, tier tip with a progress bar, summary, payment methods.\n12. **Ödeme:** steps, address radio cards, payment methods (bank transfer/EFT, corporate card, 60-day open account), tax ID / PO, internal approval flow.\n13. **Sipariş Onayı & Takip:** success banner, escrow status, timeline, live location card (text alternative), e-invoice.\n14. **Mesajlar:** conversation list, chat log (role=log), live translation TR ⇄ EN, attachment.\n15. **Alıcı Paneli:** KPI cards, spend chart (with an accessible table), orders table, approval queue, AI savings insight.\n16. **Giriş:** passkey first, e-mail/password (show/hide, autocomplete, paste allowed), magic link, SSO, no CAPTCHA. On TV: device code K74QX plus QR.\n17. **Kurumsal Kayıt:** progress 1/3, tax ID (VKN) → \"Bilgileri getir\" auto-fill, KVKK consent.\n18. **Ticaret Güvencesi:** hero plus stat card, 4 steps, coverage, FAQ accordion.\n19. **Tedarikçi Olun:** dark hero with metrics, features, 3 pricing plans.\n20. **Yardım Merkezi:** AI assistant search with topic chips, topics, contact (consistent help).\n21. **Hakkımızda:** metrics, values, careers band.\n22. **404, Bakım & Boş Durumlar:** 404 with search, empty state, planned maintenance (role=status), offline (role=alert).\n\n**Sample data:** use the same fictional content as the reference. It includes:\n- 10 sectors\n- 14 products (organic cotton jersey, industrial mixer, olive oil, porcelain tile, corrugated boxes, LED panel, solid oak table, PET granules, brake disc, rose water, leather briefcase, Turkish coffee, Afyon marble, marine rope), each with tiered prices, MOQ and a match score\n- 6 flash events\n- 5 suppliers\n\nEvery state is a variant:\n\n- **Button:** type (Primary, Secondary, Tertiary, Danger) × state (Default, Hover, Pressed, Focus, Disabled, Loading). The nested icon is swappable.\n- **IconButton:** ghost/tonal/outline/surface × Default/Focus/Disabled.\n- **Input, Select and Textarea:** Default, Focus, Filled, Error, Disabled.\n- **Checkbox:** Checked/Unchecked/Indeterminate × Default/Focus/Disabled.\n- **Radio**, **Switch**.\n- **Chip:** Filter/AI suggestion × Default/Selected.\n- **Badge tones:** Neutral, Brand, Success, Warning, Danger, AI, Premium.\n- **Toast** (success/error/info), **Tooltip**, **Kbd**, **Avatar**, **Rating**, **Stepper**, **TierProgress**, **Skeleton**.\n- **Navigation:**\n  - Header: 8 separate components, one per family\n  - BottomNav (4 active-tab variants), Rail (5 active variants)\n  - Footer: compact/regular/large/xl\n  - ⌘K command palette, mega menu, filter bottom sheet\n- **Commerce:**\n  - ProductCard S/M/L/XL × Default/Hover/Loading\n  - ProductCard TV (Default/Focused)\n  - SupplierCard, EventCard S/M/L, CategoryTile, PriceTiers, AISearch S/L, CompareTray, QuoteRow (best/standard), TimelineStep (done/now/next), StatCard, EmptyState\n- **Icon library:** about 80 Phosphor UI icons in 16/20/24/32 as components, plus 18 duotone category illustrations.\n\nBuild every page on every screen from these components. Master-component changes must propagate to every instance.\n\n1. Build the foundations (tokens, library colors and typography), then the component library, then 22 pages × 22 screens.\n2. **Round 1 and round 2:**\n   - Run an automated audit over every frame: min 16px, radius ≤ 12, overflow/reflow, target size, text contrast, collapsed layers, token adherence (share of fills linked to the library).\n   - Visually inspect representative screens and answer \"where could this be improved?\".\n   - Fix what you find.\n3. **Round 3:** fix at the **master component level** and verify that the change propagates to all instances.\n\n- The approved design is implemented as code **1:1**:\n  - Tokens become CSS variables. Device families use the `data-fam` attribute (phone | phoneL | tablet | tabletL | desktop | wide | ultra | tv).\n  - Roboto, and Phosphor via an SVG sprite containing only the icons in use.\n  - **Static HTML/CSS/JS with no dependencies.**\n  - Use the tool's code export (A: JSX/Tailwind; B: React/HTML/CSS and others) wherever it helps. Measure how faithful the output is, and write the gaps into the report.\n- **URL structure:**\n  - `/<cluster>/<screen>/<page>.html`, for example `/mobil-dikey/320/urun.html` or `/tv/4k/odeme.html`\n  - 22 × 22 = 484 screen files\n  - an index page for each cluster and for each screen\n- **Root page = viewer:**\n  - **Left side:** vertical tabs; cluster headings with that cluster's screens (320, 360, 375…) stacked below each.\n  - **Right side:** the selected screen's live, clickable design at real device size in an iframe, scaled to fit the panel (with a \"fit / 100%\" toggle).\n  - **Top:** page chips, \"open in new tab\".\n  - **URL hash:** `#cluster/screen/page` (shareable, back/forward work).\n  - **Narrow screens:** below 900px, a dropdown.\n  - **Embedded screens:** a device screen loaded inside the viewer hides its device bar (`embed`).\n- **Every screen page:** a top device bar for cluster/screen/page switching, a \"fit\" button (5K/8K/TV), and a theme button. The default theme is light.\n- **Interactions:**\n  - ⌘K, mega menu, filter sheet, AI search, stepper\n  - compare checkbox → toast\n  - theme switching\n  - TV spatial navigation with the arrow keys; initial focus lands on the active tab\n- **Pre-publish QA:**\n  - Load every one of the 484 screens at its real width.\n  - Check: 0 horizontal overflow, 0 text under 16px, 0 radius over 12px, 0 unlabelled form controls, exactly one h1 per page, 0 broken internal links. Grids use `minmax(0,1fr)`, and rows of buttons wrap.\n  - Take headless screenshots of representative screens (320, 390, 844×390, 768, 1440, 2560, TV) and review them.\n  - Cache-bust asset URLs with a content hash (`?v=<hash>`).\n- **Publish:** GitHub Pages; the root is the viewer; the report lives at `/rapor/`.\n\n### A) open-pencil/open-pencil\n\n- Work files: `.fig` (read/write) or `.pen`.\n- Drive it through the MCP server (`openpencil-mcp`, 100+ tools; `claude mcp add --scope user open-pencil -- openpencil-mcp`), the desktop app, or the CLI (`openpencil`).\n- Use these capabilities:\n  - components/variants, auto layout and design tokens through the Figma Plugin API\n  - an XPath query plus lint pass (naming, layout, accessibility) as part of the audit\n  - token export into the frontend's CSS variables\n  - JSX/Tailwind export for comparison\n- **Measure:**\n  - fidelity of the `.fig` round trip (can it be opened in Figma?)\n  - scale under 22 × 22 frames and around 600 components\n  - batch limits of the MCP tools\n  - write latency\n\n### B) ZSeven-W/openpencil\n\n- Work files: `.op` (JSON, human-readable, git-diffable). Commit every stage as a separate PR-like commit.\n- Drive it through the MCP (`op` CLI plus the one-click MCP setup for Claude Code) or the desktop app.\n- **Agent Teams:** the orchestrator splits a page into regions (hero, filters, grid, footer…) and parallel agents draw them.\n  - Assign one agent per cluster or per page group.\n  - Record overlaps, token drift and conflicts between parallel agents.\n- **Code export:** compare the React+Tailwind and HTML+CSS output with the hand-written frontend.\n- Built-in Git: branch → merge; measure three-way merge on `.op` files.\n- Store API keys only in local, secure configuration. Never write them into the repo or into the web version's localStorage.\n- **Measure:** parallel-agent speed-up, consistency (same token or component used for the same thing), and export fidelity.\n\n- **Evidence:** every finding is labelled UYUM (compatible), KISMİ (partial) or DİRENÇ (resistance), with its evidence.\n- **Examples from the Penpot reference**, to check for the equivalent in this tool:\n  - 100 KB body limit\n  - 120-second timeout with no cancellation\n  - heartbeat loss while the tab is hidden\n  - flex hug/fill collapse\n  - `resize()` resetting sizing\n  - listing only one component per variant group\n  - no way to rename the file\n  - no empty text allowed\n  - fuzzy font lookup\n- **Metrics:** total calls, success rate, p50/p95 duration per frame, largest request, error types, shape count.\n- **Comparison table:** Penpot + MCP vs this tool, across the same 20 dimensions (setup, connection, headless operation, scale, component/variant API, token API, export, git-friendliness, error messages, cancellation/queueing, etc.).\n- **Conclusion:** where the tool is \"enterprise ready\" and where it is still immature, plus recommendations.\n\n- [ ] New repo created, MIT licensed, clean commits (policy in §1.9)\n- [ ] Tool files in `design/`: tokens + component library + 22 pages × 22 screens\n- [ ] 3 improvement rounds done (the third at the master-component level), each summarized in the report\n- [ ] `docs/`: viewer + 484 screen pages + `/rapor/`, published on GitHub Pages, all URLs returning 200\n- [ ] QA: 484/484 screens clean (overflow, 16px, radius, labels, h1, links)\n- [ ] `measurements/`: calls.jsonl + findings + metrics + Penpot comparison\n- [ ] README: live link, structure, how to run, licenses (Phosphor MIT, Roboto Apache-2.0)"
